\begin_layout Standard
This is a very one-dimensional view of the world.
 There are as such two limitations 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Positioning of actors.
 For example,
 whether Iran is going to attack or not may be known with varied accuracy but the parties interested to know this are positioned to benefit or lose from this event in different ways.
 They receive information differently also because they invest in their resources differently.
 It's not merely the degree of belief but the degree of knowledge - since every investor knows more about themselves.
 It's one thing to say that markets events are known with varying degree of knowledge - but another to say that the investors influence each other and have a different sets of information about each other - as they act to influence each other.
 
\end_layout

